<title>FRANCE: EU accepts daily bids for 217,000 T wheat exports.</title>
<headline>EU accepts daily bids for 217,000 T wheat exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday accepted bids submitted through a daily channel on Tuesday for 217,000 tonnes of soft wheat exports with a nil value licence, European grain officials said.</p>
<p>The decision to accept the bids came as the EU shut the tender for exports through the parallel weekly tender, a move that all but closes the July/June export campaign.</p>
<p>The daily system remains open with a nil value refund, which means traders can take out short validity licences whose value can be changed before they are used, officials said.</p>
<p>The Commission has a three-day right of veto over such bids.</p>
</text>
